<header><p class="st-kicker">kingdom · Balkans and Hungary</p><h1 class="st-title">Kingdom of Bulgaria</h1><p class="st-meta">1908 CE – 1946 CE · capital Sofia</p></header>
<p class="st-teaser">Bulgarian tsardom that fought on the losing side of three wars in search of Macedonia and Thrace, before its monarchy was abolished under Soviet influence.</p>
<div class="st-body"><div class="st-text"><h2>Origins</h2><p>On 5 October 1908 Prince Ferdinand of the <a class="enc-link st-link" href="/state/principality-of-bulgaria">Principality of Bulgaria</a> proclaimed independence from the <a class="enc-link st-link" href="/empire/ottoman-empire">Ottoman Empire</a> and took the title of tsar. <a class="enc-link st-link" href="/state/bulgaria">Bulgaria</a> joined the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/balkan-league">Balkan League</a> and won the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/first-balkan-war">First Balkan War</a> in 1912, but its attack on <a class="enc-link st-link" href="/state/serbia">Serbia</a> and <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/greece">Greece</a> in 1913 led to defeat in the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/second-balkan-war">Second Balkan War</a> and loss of most of its gains.</p><h2>Rule and society</h2><p>Hoping to win <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/macedonia-region">Macedonia</a>, <a class="enc-link st-link" href="/state/bulgaria">Bulgaria</a> joined the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/central-powers">Central Powers</a> in 1915; defeat in 1918 brought Ferdinand's abdication in favour of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/boris-iii-of-bulgaria">Boris III</a> and the harsh <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/treaty-of-neuilly-sur-seine">Treaty of Neuilly</a>. <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/aleksandar-stamboliyski">Aleksandar Stamboliyski's</a> agrarian government was overthrown in 1923, and Boris ruled personally from 1935. As an <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/axis-powers">Axis</a> ally from 1941 <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/bulgaria">Bulgaria</a> occupied <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/vardar-macedonia">Yugoslav Macedonia</a> and <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/thrace">Thrace</a>; <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/jews">Jews</a> of the old kingdom were saved from <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/deportation">deportation</a> in 1943.</p><h2>Decline and legacy</h2><p>After <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/boris-iii-of-bulgaria">Boris</a> died in 1943, the Soviet army entered <a class="enc-link st-link" href="/state/bulgaria">Bulgaria</a> in September 1944 and the communist-led <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/fatherland-front-bulgaria">Fatherland Front</a> seized power. A referendum in 1946 abolished the monarchy, and the boy king <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/simeon-saxe-coburg-gotha">Simeon II</a> went into exile, leading to the <a class="enc-link st-link" href="/state/peoples-republic-of-bulgaria">People's Republic of Bulgaria</a>.</p></div><aside class="st-side"><figure class="st-fig"><img src="/images/states/kingdom-of-bulgaria.jpg" alt="Kingdom of Bulgaria" width="320" height="192"><figcaption>Image: SKopp · Public domain · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Flag_of_Bulgaria.svg" target="_blank" rel="noopener">source</a></figcaption></figure><dl class="st-facts"><dt>Years</dt><dd>1908 CE – 1946 CE</dd><dt>Century</dt><dd><a href="/centuries/20th-century">20th century</a></dd><dt>Type</dt><dd>kingdom</dd><dt>Character</dt><dd>bureaucratic</dd><dt>Capital</dt><dd>Sofia</dd><dt>Rulers</dt><dd>Ferdinand I, Boris III, Simeon II</dd><dt>Religion</dt><dd>Bulgarian Orthodox Christianity</dd><dt>Language</dt><dd>Bulgarian</dd><dt>Today</dt><dd><a href="/countries/bulgaria">Bulgaria</a></dd><dt>Also</dt><dd>Tsardom of Bulgaria, Third Bulgarian State</dd></dl><figure class="st-locator"><a href="/atlas?year=1927&amp;focus=kingdom-of-bulgaria" aria-label="Kingdom of Bulgaria on the atlas"><svg class="map map-loc" viewBox="5244 660 640 512" role="img" aria-label="Map: where Kingdom of Bulgaria lay"><image href="/maps/world.svg" x="0" y="0" width="10000" height="4393"/><path class="map-tie" d="M5564 916L5564 916M5564 916L5564 916M5564 916L5621 967"/><path class="map-dot-n" d="M5564 916h0M5564 916h0M5621 967h0"/><path class="map-dot-halo"